dtlogin: read the password from the shadow file on SVR4.

dtlogin's generic Authenticate compares the typed password with
getpwnam()'s pw_passwd, which on a shadowed system is a placeholder:
it fetches the real one with getspnam() only on Linux (and with
getpwnam_shadow() on OpenBSD). System V Release 4 keeps the passwords in
/etc/shadow, read with getspnam() from <shadow.h>, so every login was
"Login incorrect". The Linux branch is taken on SVR4 too. dtsession's
screen lock already reads the shadow file on SVR4.

--- a/programs/dtlogin/sysauth.c	2026-11-20 12:03:13
+++ b/programs/dtlogin/sysauth.c	2026-11-20 12:03:13
@@ -117,7 +117,7 @@
 #define generic
 #endif
 
-#if defined(__linux__)
+#if defined(__linux__) || defined(SVR4)
 #    include <shadow.h>
 #endif
 
@@ -1010,9 +1010,9 @@
 
     p = getpwnam(name);
     
-#if defined(__linux__)
-    /*
-     * Use the Linux Shadow Password system to get the crypt()ed password
+#if defined(__linux__) || defined(SVR4)
+    /*
+     * Use the shadow password file (Linux, SVR4) to get the crypt()ed password
      */
     if(p) {
         struct spwd *s = getspnam(name);
